{"chunk_id": "94eb901a1995", "text": "Sita, alone in the forest while Rama and Lakshmana are away, receives a visitor disguised as a mendicant\u2014Ravana, who has come intending to abduct her. Bound by duty to treat a supposed brahmin with respect, she introduces herself and recounts the story of Rama\u2019s exile: Kaikeyi\u2019s demand, Dasaratha\u2019s reluctant obedience, and Rama\u2019s steadfast acceptance of banishment. Ravana then drops his disguise in words, declaring himself the feared king of the titans and tempting Sita with wealth and queenship in Lanka. Sita responds with fierce devotion and scorn, praising Rama\u2019s greatness while mocking Ravana\u2019s arrogance through vivid comparisons. The exchange heightens the tension before the impending abduction, revealing Sita\u2019s moral courage and unwavering loyalty in the face of intimidation.\nSita recounts her exile to the disguised Ravana, who reveals himself and tries to seduce her, but she fiercely rejects and insults him.\nThemes: loyalty to Rama, temptation and defiance, identity revelation, abduction foreshadowing, moral steadfastness", "vector": [0.006601549219340086, -0.029142452403903008, 0.006070237141102552, 0.004137590527534485, -0.010334014892578125, 0.019472576677799225, -0.040804747492074966, -0.01245926134288311, -0.026724983006715775, -0.022766711190342903, 0.015726828947663307, 0.002065474633127451, 0.013707844540476799, 0.010360579937696457, -0.01571354642510414, 0.005070706829428673, 0.04069848358631134, -0.00894596241414547, 0.026113975793123245, -0.024267666041851044, -0.0007097993511706591, -0.007557910401374102, -0.010792271234095097, 0.008567403070628643, -0.031320828944444656, -0.009430784732103348, 0.02673826739192009, -0.03671364486217499, 0.027973566204309464, -0.01728091575205326, -0.021066512912511826, -0.009530405513942242, -0.003772313706576824, -0.004453056957572699, -0.02293938770890236, 0.019671820104122162, -0.009450708515942097, -0.01174199115484953, 0.012206888